BE-293: RETRIGGER_VALIDATE_DID_DOCUMENT must resume IDENTITY_WALLET in IN_PROGRESS (not TO_DO)

Base: ARENA2036/portal-backend ad459ee711ecaa9a43535a513bd9db83b640a8ff (deployed on Alpha); also applies to
feat/BE-293-portal-integration f5badda90. Upstream eclipse-tractusx/portal-backend main has the same mapping.

Defect: POST /api/administration/registration/application/{id}/retrigger-validate-did set the IDENTITY_WALLET
checklist entry to TO_DO. VALIDATE_DID_DOCUMENT (DidDocumentValidationBusinessLogic) only runs while that
entry is IN_PROGRESS - the state CREATE_IDENTITY_HUB_WALLET / the DIM callback leave it in - so the retriggered
step failed immediately, scheduled no further retrigger, and left the application unrecoverable through the API.
Fix: map the retrigger to IN_PROGRESS, as RETRIGGER_BUSINESS_PARTNER_NUMBER_PULL and the activation retriggers
already do. Only the manual retrigger path changes; the wallet is never recreated (the retrigger schedules only
VALIDATE_DID_DOCUMENT; a successful validation schedules only TRANSMIT_BPN_DID).

Affected image: portal-administration-service only (the mapping is read solely by
Administration.Service RegistrationBusinessLogic.TriggerChecklistAsync). Worker, migrations, schema: unchanged.

Apply: git apply --index ci/portal-backend-retrigger-validate-did.patch   (from the portal-backend root)
